    {
      "id": "p0108-b007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Before he released Undertale in English, Toby already hoped to release a Japanese version of the game someday. But he was concerned that the connection between the name \"Sans\" and the English \"Comic Sans\" font might be lost on Japanese players. For this reason, 8-4’s localization team initially suggested naming Sans \"Pop\", in reference to a similarly popular-but-notorious Japanese font known as \"Sōeikaku Pop-tai\".",
        "raw": "Before he released Undertale in English, Toby already hoped to release\na Japanese version of the game someday. But he was concerned that the\nconnection between the name \"Sans\" and the English \"Comic Sans\" font might\nbe Jost on Japanese players. For this reason, 8-4's localization team initially\nsuggested naming Sans \"Pop\", in reference to a similarly popular-but-notorious\nJapanese font known as \"Siieikaku Pop-tai\".",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29765612,
          0.43052143,
          0.90867319,
          0.53332857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.29473382,
          0.42980714,
          0.91071676,
          0.5344
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          18,
          19,
          20,
          21,
          22,
          23
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "在 Undertale 英语版发行之前，Toby 就希望有朝一日推出日语版。但他担心日本玩家无法理解“Sans”这个名字与英文字体“Comic Sans”之间的联系。因此，8-4 的本地化团队最初建议把 Sans 改名为“Pop”，对应同样流行、同样恶名在外的日文字体“Sōeikaku Pop-tai”。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 11,
            "italic": true,
            "lang": "en"
          }
        ]
