    {
      "id": "p0108-b010",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The name \"Pop\" had drawbacks, however: early fans were already attached to Sans' name, the Siieikaku Pop-tai font was a slightly more professional font than Comic Sans, and the name had a very different ring to it. So it wasn't too surprising when the team decided to revert \"Pop\" back to \"Sans\" a few months before the Japanese game's release.",
        "raw": "The name \"Pop\" had drawbacks, however: early fans were already attached\nto Sans' name, the Siieikaku Pop-tai font was a slightly more professional font\nthan Comic Sans, and the name had a very different ring to it. So it wasn't too\nsurprising when the team decided to revert \"Pop\" back to \"Sans\" a few months\nbefore the Japanese game's release.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29906618,
          0.70458571,
          0.90482107,
          0.78930714
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.29473382,
          0.70387143,
          0.91071676,
          0.79037857
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          44,
          45,
          46,
          47,
          48
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "不过，“Pop”也有缺点：早期粉丝已经对 Sans 的名字产生了感情，Sōeikaku Pop-tai 比 Comic Sans 略显专业，而且新名字听起来很不一样。因此，团队在日语版发行前几个月决定把“Pop”改回“Sans”，也就并不令人意外了。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
